.TH IO_FREE 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
iob_free \- Free an I/O batch buffer

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/iob_internal.h>

.IB void
.IB iob_free(
.IB io_batch* b
.IB );

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBiob_free\fR function frees an I/O batch buffer. This function is used to clean up resources associated with an I/O batch buffer when it is no longer needed.

The function takes the following parameter:

.IB b
Pointer to the I/O batch buffer.

The function does not return any value.

The function is part of the \fBiob\fR library, which provides a framework for managing I/O operations in batch mode.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBiob_free\fR function to free an I/O batch buffer:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/iob.h>

int main() {
  io_batch batch;
  io_batch_init(&batch);

  // Add data to the batch buffer
  iob_adds(&batch, "Hello, World!");
  iob_adds(&batch, "This is a test.");

  // Process the batch buffer
  while (iob_bytesleft(&batch) > 0) {
    iob_execute(&batch);
  }

  // Free the I/O batch buffer
  iob_free(&batch);

  printf("I/O batch buffer freed\n");

  return 0;
}
.nef